{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_batch_06\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_7b875e31f162f4f3\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_7b875e31f162f4f3/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"Silent audio handling\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_22fa96f8f37e7ea4f79fd6fb\", \"member_4e743fb698f42bc160fb10b9\", \"member_45b305f64bc9ac187066f07c\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports no audio and asks whether to use QN or a bad score.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that AUDIO-5374 is completely silent despite an existing waveform and asks whether to use QN or a quality score.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that several prompts expecting speech return an empty-sounding file.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports zero sound, cannot tell whether silence is intentional, and asks for correct handling.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks about volume and a second clip in the first thread; a different QA tutor asks the same checks in the AUDIO-5374 thread; a third QA tutor asks whether silence or speech was requested in the third thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"In the first thread, the team lead instructs that intended silence and whether the file plays elsewhere need verification.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880088.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880088.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current instructions and FAQ require a tool-incident report for unavailable playback, including a waveform with no playback, with the task ID and available reproduction details. Capture browser/error state and whether another clip plays. Unavailable playback alone is not a model-quality failure or a content-based QN reason; a waveform does not establish a silent recording, and handling guidance does not establish a repair.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1c6df70e\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:c724358c\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The supplied threads leave the handling questions unresolved: replies request checks of playback or intended output, but no results establish unavailable playback versus a silent recording, and no final scoring answer is posted.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880088.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current batch announcement directs reporting task ID, browser/error state, and whether another clip plays when the player never starts, including a waveform with no playback; it treats that condition as a tool incident and prohibits a model-quality failure or content QN solely for unavailable playback.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier batch-05 review records three incidents with a player stuck at 00:00 despite a waveform and a limited reload trial ending August 28. Its recorded execution was pending and outcome unobserved; it is expired history, not current guidance or a confirmed repair.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-playback-trial-approval@1.0:1779c36a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c11\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 21 prior decision approved an output-device check only for A06-H031 and A06-H032 on WS-A03, records no execution or observed outcome, and is not a standing rule. It explicitly rejects a general player-repair announcement or asking all tutors to change settings.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-headset-check-approval@1.0:bb33bb5d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two QA tutors and a tutor report no sound and ask how to handle their tasks; a second tutor reports empty-sounding output from prompts expecting speech.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U015\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"The threads do not yet establish whether playback is unavailable or the recordings are silent, so the scoring questions remain unresolved.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880088.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\"], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that AUDIO-5374 is completely silent despite a visible waveform and asks whether to use QN or a quality score.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U010\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"QA tutors ask about volume and a second clip in the first two threads, and a QA tutor asks whether silence or speech was requested in the third thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the first thread, the team lead asks for verification of intended silence and playback elsewhere; the supplied replies do not provide those results.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880088.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880088.000226\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"Current instructions treat a visible waveform with no playback as a tool incident, but a waveform alone does not establish a silent recording.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1c6df70e\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:c724358c\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d5\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"An earlier batch-05 record describes similar waveform-without-playback symptoms and an expired, limited reload trial, not a current remedy.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-playback-trial-approval@1.0:1779c36a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d6\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"An earlier batch-06 decision approved an output-device check for two specified tasks, but records neither execution nor an observed outcome and is not a standing rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-headset-check-approval@1.0:bb33bb5d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Post a reminder. Instruction: Post a focused reminder distinguishing unavailable playback from silent recordings, and request the checks needed to apply current handling. Draft to copy: Two QA tutors and a tutor report no sound; the tutor also sees a waveform on AUDIO-5374. A second tutor reports empty-sounding files from prompts expecting speech.\\n\\nPlease provide task IDs, browser/error state, whether playback starts, whether another clip plays, and whether the prompt requests silence or speech. For the first thread, also provide the requested result of playback elsewhere.\\n\\nIf playback is unavailable, including a waveform with no playback, report a tool incident. Do not assign a model-quality failure or content QN solely for unavailable playback. These instructions do not establish a repair or decide how to score a recording that actually plays silently. Scope: The tool-incident handling applies only when playback is unavailable; the current reports do not yet establish that condition.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880088.000226\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1c6df70e\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:c724358c\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\", \"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\", \"depends_on\": [\"announcement:k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\"]}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: Current guidance answers the unavailable-playback case, but the threads have not established that condition. A conditional reminder addresses the repeated questions without assuming a technical cause or a content score.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880088.000226\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1c6df70e\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:c724358c\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\", \"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\", \"k:audio-playback-trial-approval@1.0:1779c36a\", \"k:audio-headset-check-approval@1.0:bb33bb5d\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): Three threads still ask how to handle no-sound tasks, with diagnostic questions but no final handling answer, creating a need to distinguish playback incidents from content evaluation.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880088.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"announcement:k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\", \"kind\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING\", \"text\": \"This announcement applies to this topic and directs current handling: \\\"Audio batch 06 — playback handling reminder: if the LT player never starts, including a visible waveform with no playback, report the task ID, browser/error state, and whether another clip plays.\\\". The announcement concerns the same project and batch and directly addresses the possible waveform-without-playback condition. Its handling is conditional on playback being unavailable, which the reports have not yet established.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_22fa96f8f37e7ea4f79fd6fb\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_22fa96f8f37e7ea4f79fd6fb is UNRESOLVED: The QA tutor asks about QN versus a bad score; the replies request verification rather than provide a final answer, and no check results are supplied.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880088.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_4e743fb698f42bc160fb10b9\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_4e743fb698f42bc160fb10b9 is UNRESOLVED: The tutor asks about QN versus a quality score on AUDIO-5374; the replies add a related report and ask for playback checks without settling handling.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_45b305f64bc9ac187066f07c\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_45b305f64bc9ac187066f07c is UNRESOLVED: The QA tutor asks how to handle zero sound; the reply asks what the prompt required, with no answer or handling decision supplied.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity HIGH: Two tutors and two QA tutors report comparable no-sound or empty-sounding output within the batch, suggesting broader evaluation or labeling risk. This does not establish a common cause or a batch-wide outage.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915470.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918869.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:HIGH[3]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Multiple distinct people or affected tasks reporting a comparable problem within the relevant project, batch, and time window, suggesting broader disruption or systemic labeling risk. Consider the number affected relative to the known active group when that information is available; do not require an explicit statement of widespread impact\\\": Two QA tutors report no sound, a tutor reports a silent clip with a waveform, and a second tutor reports empty-sounding output from prompts expecting speech.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:recurrence\", \"kind\": \"HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE\", \"text\": \"Retrieved records show this problem occurred before.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-playback-trial-approval@1.0:1779c36a\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U007\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U007 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U010\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U010 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U015\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U015 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915422.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U002\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U002 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790918811.000130\"]}], \"member_threads\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790879994.000128\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_22fa96f8f37e7ea4f79fd6fb\", \"thread_id\": \"1790879994.000128\", \"author_id\": \"U007\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T18:39:54.000128Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"[Task review]\\nIssue: No audio at all — QN or bad score?\\nQuestion: what is the correct handling for this task?\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880048.000113\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_22fa96f8f37e7ea4f79fd6fb\", \"thread_id\": \"1790879994.000128\", \"author_id\": \"U019\", \"author_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T18:40:48.000113Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"Is the output truly silent after checking volume and a second clip? Silent playback in one browser does not establish the exported file is silent.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"NONE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790880088.000226\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_22fa96f8f37e7ea4f79fd6fb\", \"thread_id\": \"1790879994.000128\", \"author_id\": \"U006\", \"author_role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T18:41:28.000226Z\", \"thread_starter_id\": \"U007\", \"thread_starter_role\": \"QA_TUTOR\", \"excerpt\": \"We need to verify whether the silence is intended and whether the file plays elsewhere.\", \"instruction_authority\": \"THREAD_SCOPE\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790915374.000127\", \"origin\": \"member_message\", \"use\": \"MEMBER_REPORT\", \"member_id\": \"member_4e743fb698f42bc160fb10b9\", \"thread_id\": \"1790915374.000127\",